      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/clio/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s first post office opened in 1860, long before the Civil War, marking Clio as a communication center in the frontier.",
